1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,480
In 1477, outside the gates of the Jossian capital, a group of shamans performed a ritual.

2
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:10,480
Someone reported it.

3
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:13,000
The court asked who had ordered it.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,160
The answer, the palace had.

5
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:19,520
The king's own wet nurse and a royal eunuch had gone there to pray.

6
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:25,320
The king's response was a single line recorded in the annals, do not do this again.

7
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:29,000
That is the whole story of Jossian in one exchange.

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:36,280
For 500 years, this Confucian state outlawed shamanism, taxed it, exiled its practitioners,

9
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:38,400
and wrote laws against it.

10
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:43,360
And for 500 years, the palace kept calling them back.

11
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:49,800
Korean shamanism, musok, is older than Buddhism, Confucianism, or Christianity in Korea.

12
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:55,320
Its practitioners are the mutang, usually women, who speak for spirits and perform the gut,

13
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:58,640
drumming, dancing, and negotiation with the dead.

14
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:04,920
The Jossian dynasty was built on near Confucianism, and it saw all of this as Yumsa.

15
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:06,320
Lued rights.

16
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:07,840
Not just wrong.

17
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:08,840
Disorderly.

18
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:17,000
In 1431, the censorate petitioned King Sejong with a complaint that sounds remarkably modern.

19
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:22,280
Channons were living inside the capital, and noble women were visiting them constantly.

20
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:27,760
Sick people were being gathered in their houses, spreading disease through the neighborhoods.

21
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:29,520
The fix was simple.

22
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:31,040
Move them out.

23
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:35,680
Channons were pushed beyond the city walls, into settlements that the records literally

24
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:37,720
call Maju cry.

25
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:39,000
Channon villages.

26
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:44,880
The most famous stood outside the South Gate, and along the Han River at Noyangjin.

27
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:48,200
They were also pushed down the social order.

28
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:50,520
Channons were classified as Sassan.

29
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:55,040
Lobam ranked alongside butchers, actors, and slaves.

30
00:01:55,040 --> 00:02:01,160
In the early dynasty, they and their descendants were barred from receiving state land.

31
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:04,240
Here is where the story stops being a simple ban.

32
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:06,800
The palace had its own shamans.

33
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:11,660
They were called Gungmoo, state shamans, and they were housed in an office inside the

34
00:02:11,660 --> 00:02:14,680
palace grounds, the Seongchang.

35
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:16,200
The Star Shrine.

36
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:20,720
Their job was to pray for the royal family and to avert disaster.

37
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:22,600
This was not a secret.

38
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:26,280
It was an institution with a budget and a staff.

39
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:30,480
And when the country needed rain, the state called the shamans.

40
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:37,520
In 1410, King Tijong gathered 70 shamans at Beagaxon to pray for rain.

41
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:45,320
In 1436, King Sejong gave shamans rice to perform rain rites, and the record notes that

42
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:46,960
the rain came.

43
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:50,120
Again and again, the annals show the same pattern.

44
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:56,360
The Confucian state condemning shamanic ritual in public and requesting it in private.

45
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:59,760
The Star Shrine survived for over a century.

46
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:07,040
In 1503, King Yonesungun, no friend of Confucian officials, stated plainly that the office

47
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:11,320
of state shamans was ancient and should continue.

48
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:16,600
In 1478, King Seongchang lost patience.

49
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:21,680
The shamans had been expelled from the capital, and then they had simply come back.

50
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:23,840
The prohibition had loosened.

51
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:29,160
They were practicing in the city again, openly, without the slightest hesitation.

52
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:34,320
His order to the censorate is one of the most revealing lines in the annals.

53
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:38,000
It has become the custom, the lewd rites flourish.

54
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,500
The ignorant crowd flocks to them.

55
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:43,200
It cannot be left unprohibited.

56
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:44,520
Read that again.

57
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:48,520
It is the sound of a state admitting that its law is not working.

58
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:50,680
So the laws got harsher.

59
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:54,040
Shamans caught inside the capital were punished.

60
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:56,960
Officials who failed to arrest them were dismissed.

61
00:03:56,960 --> 00:04:01,960
And the state began to tax them, the muse, partly to squeeze them out of business, partly

62
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:03,960
because it needed the money.

63
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:11,680
In 1464, the government ordered a register of every shaman, compiled every three years,

64
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:14,760
so the tax could be collected properly.

65
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:17,040
Later records list the rates.

66
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:22,320
The chief state shaman paid nine June, an ordinary shaman paid one.

67
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:30,880
And yet, in 1684, a shaman named Makry was caught inside the palace, performing rituals,

68
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:33,520
and wearing the king's own dragon robe.

69
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:36,680
She was sentenced to exile on an island.

70
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:44,120
In 1743, King Yeonju signed a law ordering any shaman who entered the palace in royal

71
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:47,280
robes to be banished to a remote island.

72
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:50,280
By then, the pattern was unmistakable.

73
00:04:50,280 --> 00:04:54,680
Every generation passed a new law against the same practice.

74
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:59,200
You do not need a new law for something that has stopped happening.

75
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:05,400
Because the ban was aimed at the wrong target, the state could legislate where a shaman lived.

76
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:12,920
It could not legislate why people went to one, consider what the 1431 petition actually

77
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:14,680
complained about.

78
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:17,760
Noble women visiting shaman houses.

79
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:19,240
Not peasants.

80
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:20,880
Not the uneducated.

81
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:26,200
The wives of the elite slipping out of the capital to ask about a sick child a difficult

82
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:29,800
birth, a husband's career, a dead parent.

83
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:31,880
The annals are full of this.

84
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:36,000
A queen dowager calls for a shaman when the king falls ill.

85
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,560
A royal concubine sends for one.

86
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:44,480
A crown prince's illness becomes a shamanic ritual conducted by the palace itself.

87
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:48,400
And there was a practical reason shamans were hard to erase.

88
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:50,720
They were also the medical system.

89
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:55,760
The status signed shamans to the H. Waylin Seo, the public clinic for the poor, where

90
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:59,280
they treated patients alongside physicians.

91
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:01,680
The tax they paid helped fund it.

92
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:06,520
For people with no access to a doctor, the shaman was not superstition.

93
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:08,760
She was the only help available.

94
00:06:08,760 --> 00:06:09,760
Grief.

95
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:10,760
Illness.

96
00:06:10,760 --> 00:06:11,760
Infertility.

97
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:12,760
Sudden death.

98
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:16,160
The things a confusion bureaucracy had no ritual for.

99
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:18,840
Shamanism had a ritual for all of them.

100
00:06:18,840 --> 00:06:20,880
You can out war a practice.

101
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:23,440
You cannot out war grief.

102
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:27,720
By the 18th century, the state had stopped trying to win.

103
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:35,280
In 1745, Yeonju formally abolished the last official shamanic rights from the register

104
00:06:35,280 --> 00:06:37,120
of state ceremonies.

105
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:45,720
In 1763, the censorate asked once more to expel the shamans from Seoul, and the king agreed.

106
00:06:45,720 --> 00:06:47,320
And still they came.

107
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:53,360
In the final decades of the dynasty, the most powerful woman in Korea, Queen Min, the future

108
00:06:53,360 --> 00:06:58,240
Empress Myeon Seong, kept shamans close enough that two of them were granted honorary

109
00:06:58,240 --> 00:07:00,080
noble titles.

110
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:06,680
When Japan annexed Korea in 1910, the new colonial government tried again, classifying

111
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:09,600
shamanism as primitive superstition.

112
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:16,200
Then the military governments of the 1960s and 70s tried again, shutting down shrines

113
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:18,320
and calling it backward.

114
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:20,320
Each time, the same result.

115
00:07:20,320 --> 00:07:23,000
Today, shamanism is not a relic.

116
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,000
It is a working profession.

117
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:30,560
Moudang's council clients perform gut for the dead and appear on television.

118
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:36,640
Estimates of their number range wildly from tens of thousands to hundreds of thousands.

119
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:39,400
But the more telling fact is cultural.

120
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:44,880
When a Korean film wants to talk about grief, guilt, and the unburied dead, it reaches

121
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:46,040
for the shaman.

122
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:55,440
The whaling, in 2016, exhumor, in 2024, both films are built on concepts that the Joss-in

123
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:59,080
state spent 500 years trying to erase.

124
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:01,720
Sal, spiritual contamination.

125
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:03,880
One hunt, the restless dead.

126
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:08,600
Han Sinbion, the spirit sickness that is said to choose a shaman, whether she wants it

127
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:10,320
or not.

128
00:08:10,320 --> 00:08:14,120
Which brings us back to the thing the laws could never touch.

129
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:18,160
In the tradition, a moudang does not decide to become one.

130
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:19,920
The spirits decide.

131
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:26,760
The sign is Sinbion, unexplained illness, seizures, hallucinations, nightmares, a body

132
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:29,040
that medicine cannot fix.

133
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:34,920
The cure is Nairim, an initiation ritual in which the person accepts the spirit.

134
00:08:34,920 --> 00:08:39,360
Refuse, the tradition says, and the illness worsens.

135
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:41,840
Some accounts say people died.

136
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:45,360
One psychiatry has another name for parts of this.

137
00:08:45,360 --> 00:08:47,520
It also has patience.

138
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:53,920
That tension, illness or calling, diagnosis or destiny is why the story never resolves.

139
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:57,080
The state could classify shamans as lowborn.

140
00:08:57,080 --> 00:09:01,960
It could tax them, exile them, and write them out of official ceremony.

141
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:06,240
It could not answer the question they were being asked.

142
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:12,880
500 years of laws, 500 years of the same ritual, performed just outside the gate.

143
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:16,560
The kings of Josian were not fighting a superstition.

144
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:21,800
They were fighting the fact that, in the dark, when someone is dying or gone, people want

145
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:24,280
someone to speak to the other side.

146
00:09:24,280 --> 00:09:25,920
The state had laws.

147
00:09:25,920 --> 00:09:28,040
The shamans had an answer.

148
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:33,040
If you want more of the records the official histories tried to bury, subscribe.

149
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:38,920
Next, the king who drove the Confucian scholars out of the palace and filled it with shamans

150
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:39,920
instead.

